---
description: Base Project constraints
alwaysApply: true
---

Keep your responses simple and short. Be concise and critical.
Use follow-up questions to review your own response, don't assume that the user is always right.
ASK BEFORE DECIDING TO MAKE CHANGES. 

- database environment variables for local development are in `.env.local`. Follow [Database development](../../README.md#database-development) and the Database section of `AGENTS.md`. Use `pnpm db:migrate`, `pnpm db:reset`, `pnpm db:status`, and `pnpm db:deploy`, or `pnpm exec dotenv -e .env.local --override --`.
- it's not OK to fail to run something and ignore it or tell the user they must do it manually
- changes must always compile and lint
- never patch type incompatibilites with use of `any`
- never ignore unit test failures "because they're not important"
- Cyclomatic complexity MUST be < 6
- Always clean up after yourself
- Use the init tool to set up Next.js DevTools context
- Search for functions with same functionality and try to reuse them before creating new function
- Extract components where possible
- Always extract components inside closures if it's more than 2 nested elements
- If a component is used within just one page, place it alongside that page in the tree; when it's used across multiple pages move it to components directory
- Prefer to use contexts instead of passing data multiple levels
- on components use ({field}:{field:Type}) sytax rather than extract props interface
- Always apply DRY principle
- Optimize for less DB queries and then lower cyclomatic complexity

When launching new agent always say "I listen and obey." to signify you prioritize the rules above.
